00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.710
So, important stuff first, If you’ve never
heard about it, Telltale Games is making a

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.340
narrative video game series based on A Song
of Ice and Fire.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:35.230
It’s a series, meaning instead of a linear
JRPG game like Final Fantasy that releases

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.579
sequels, the Game of Thrones game will have
seasons.

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:45.670
Inside each season new content or episodes
will be released in the form of a continuing

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:46.670
narrative.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:54.770
So think of each song of ice and fire book
as a season of the game.

00:00:54.770 --> 00:01:01.050
Seasons of the telltale game will be released
about once a year.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.190
Within each season there will be 4 to 5 episodes.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:09.640
So if one book is like a season, the entire
season will be released over the course of

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.900
a year in each of those episode installments.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:25.780
A lot of you might have played the Walking
Dead Telltale game.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:30.660
They’re getting ready to release season
3 of that.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.350
The Game of Thrones game will work exactly
like that.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:36.590
Since I’ll be doing a weekly walking dead
giveaway while I make tv videos for that show,

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:39.020
